        "Nigerian towns carry layered histories: pre-colonial capitals such as Kano, Ile-Ife and Benin City grew around walls, palaces and markets; colonial port and rail towns such as Lagos, Port Harcourt and Kaduna followed the infrastructure grid; and administrative new towns like Abuja were drawn on paper before the first block was laid. In {S}, reading a town plan reveals which layer dominates and why streets run as they do.",
