        "Three classic models organise urban structure. Burgess's concentric zone model imagines rings expanding from the core; Hoyt's sector model follows transport axes outward; Harris and Ullman's multiple nuclei model argues cities grow around several specialised centres. Lagos fits all three partially: island cores, corridor sectors toward Ikeja and Badagry, and nuclei at Apapa, Ikeja and Lekki. In {S}, the models are lenses, not laws.",
