        "Abuja's plan phased development from the central area through districts, with satellite towns such as Gwagwalada absorbing overflow. Demand outran the phases, informal settlements spread, and the administration answered with periodic clean-up and re-planning exercises. In {S}, the lesson is that a master plan is a management tool to be revised against reality, not a museum piece.",
