        "Structural wishful thinking is endemic: columns dropped off the grid below, cantilevers doubled to chase a facade idea, openings cut into shear walls. In {S}, every scheme move must be priced in load paths; a designer who cannot sketch the load path is drafting a demolition notice. Engineers sign the drawings that carry their calculations for a reason.",
