        "Convert before computing: a 6.4 centimetre length on a 1:25,000 plan is 1.6 kilometres on the ground, and a 4 square centimetre parcel at that scale is 25 hectares. Most lost marks are lost at this step, not at the clever one after. In {S} drills, write the scale, the unit chain, then the arithmetic.",
        "A drain must fall from level 52.0 at chainage 0 to no more than 1 in 150 by chainage 900; the permissible drop is 6.0 metres, exactly 1 in 150, so the design holds with no surplus. In {S} site engineering, check the fall you need against the fall the land gives before drawing the long section.",
